1
00:00:55,097 --> 00:00:59,226
TAEKANG MITAN MEDICAL CENTER

2
00:01:02,938 --> 00:01:04,899
The blood tests and X-ray look fine.

3
00:01:05,566 --> 00:01:08,611
There's no infection at the wound
and no fractures.

4
00:01:09,236 --> 00:01:11,322
The swelling and bruising
will last a few days.

5
00:01:28,380 --> 00:01:29,840
Since you are fine,

6
00:01:32,718 --> 00:01:34,637
I have to ask you.

7
00:01:37,431 --> 00:01:38,682
Jae-hee, are you a man…

8
00:01:42,061 --> 00:01:43,270
or a woman?

9
00:01:51,028 --> 00:01:51,987
I'm sorry.

10
00:01:52,071 --> 00:01:53,906
I want an answer, not an apology!

11
00:01:56,367 --> 00:01:57,827
Did you deceive me?

12
00:02:28,315 --> 00:02:29,483
Mr. Yoon.

13
00:02:30,276 --> 00:02:31,527
Wait, Mr. Yoon.

14
00:02:32,778 --> 00:02:33,696
Mr. Yoon.

15
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:37,658
I can explain.

16
00:02:42,288 --> 00:02:43,539
I'm sorry I lied to you.

17
00:02:44,331 --> 00:02:45,291
You're sorry?

18
00:02:46,292 --> 00:02:47,167
You are?

19
00:02:48,252 --> 00:02:51,839
Was it fun deceiving me
wearing those bandages?

20
00:02:52,298 --> 00:02:54,091
You pretended to be a man

21
00:02:54,174 --> 00:02:57,261
while you watched me losing my mind
over you, thinking you were a man!

22
00:02:58,596 --> 00:02:59,555
And you're sorry?

23
00:03:02,933 --> 00:03:05,311
-I had a reason…
-Mr. Yoon!

24
00:03:06,186 --> 00:03:09,315
Mr. Yoon, are you okay?

25
00:03:09,398 --> 00:03:11,692
How did the accident happen?

26
00:03:12,234 --> 00:03:13,068
Secretary Kang!

27
00:03:14,069 --> 00:03:17,406
What happened to your face?
What on earth happened?

28
00:03:18,073 --> 00:03:19,033
Just go home.

29
00:03:20,367 --> 00:03:22,912
The hospital director is on standby.

30
00:03:22,995 --> 00:03:24,663
-I'll take you there.
-Forget it.

31
00:03:25,372 --> 00:03:27,374
Just keep the press from reporting this.

32
00:03:34,089 --> 00:03:36,884
External Relations
is handling it right now.

33
00:03:52,232 --> 00:03:54,944
Is this the right place?
I think we're here.

34
00:03:56,987 --> 00:03:58,781
Well… Yes.

35
00:03:59,531 --> 00:04:01,075
Thank you for driving me home.

36
00:04:09,667 --> 00:04:12,336
I'll be off, sir.

37
00:05:03,804 --> 00:05:04,847
Mr. Yoon!

38
00:05:06,807 --> 00:05:07,975
Kang Jae-hee.

39
00:05:17,651 --> 00:05:20,612
Jae-hee, are you a man or a woman?

40
00:05:22,906 --> 00:05:24,241
Did you deceive me?

41
00:05:38,172 --> 00:05:40,424
EPISODE 9

42
00:05:45,888 --> 00:05:47,890
You lost the recording pen?

43
00:05:48,223 --> 00:05:51,643
Given they targeted the car publicly,
they were desperate.

44
00:05:51,727 --> 00:05:54,063
What about the dashcam?
They must've had one.

45
00:05:54,563 --> 00:05:57,316
They were thorough.
They took the dashcam memory card.

46
00:05:58,567 --> 00:05:59,943
What do we do now?

47
00:06:02,237 --> 00:06:04,031
What about Mr. Yoon and Mr. Kang?

48
00:06:04,114 --> 00:06:06,950
They were in an accident,
but the injuries weren't serious.

49
00:06:10,496 --> 00:06:14,208
I heard they were taken to the hospital.

50
00:06:14,416 --> 00:06:17,836
Secretary Kang was driving.
He just has minor injuries and bruises.

51
00:06:18,754 --> 00:06:20,756
Mr. Yoon was barely injured.

52
00:06:23,634 --> 00:06:25,135
It's nothing to worry about.

53
00:06:27,971 --> 00:06:29,640
Why are you so worried about them?

54
00:06:29,723 --> 00:06:32,476
Answer carefully.
I don't want to be in a love triangle.

55
00:06:35,479 --> 00:06:36,605
Don't worry, okay?

56
00:06:40,818 --> 00:06:41,777
Do you need a hand?

57
00:06:42,569 --> 00:06:44,029
I can do it alone.

58
00:07:13,976 --> 00:07:15,352
Kim Hak-ju, 30 years old.

59
00:07:15,435 --> 00:07:16,270
NA MAN-SEOK

60
00:07:16,353 --> 00:07:18,438
As part of a rehabilitation program,

61
00:07:18,522 --> 00:07:22,484
Taekang Cultural Foundation assigns
former inmates to its subsidiaries.

62
00:07:22,734 --> 00:07:23,902
He was one of them.

63
00:07:26,697 --> 00:07:30,284
I understand that former inmates with jobs
have a lower recidivism rate.

64
00:07:30,742 --> 00:07:34,246
But his resignation date bothers me.

65
00:07:35,497 --> 00:07:39,334
It lines up exactly with
the date of Han Eun-young's death…

66
00:07:41,336 --> 00:07:42,421
Kim Hak-ju is here.

67
00:07:45,048 --> 00:07:46,466
Close in on him.

68
00:07:54,183 --> 00:07:55,767
-Freeze!
-Damn it.

69
00:07:59,062 --> 00:08:00,731
Go after him!

70
00:08:09,948 --> 00:08:11,450
I knew he would come this way!

71
00:08:11,909 --> 00:08:13,368
Stop right there!

72
00:08:18,832 --> 00:08:19,666
Wan-gu!

73
00:08:32,221 --> 00:08:33,555
There we go.

74
00:08:34,556 --> 00:08:36,600
-Are you okay?
-I'm fine.

75
00:08:42,814 --> 00:08:44,149
Why isn't this working?

76
00:08:44,524 --> 00:08:47,653
Hey, just stay there.

77
00:08:52,449 --> 00:08:54,993
-Jeez. Take him!
-Yes, sir.

78
00:08:55,494 --> 00:08:58,038
You should've used this, you fools!
You'll wreck your body.

79
00:08:58,830 --> 00:08:59,665
Are you okay?

80
00:09:00,499 --> 00:09:03,043
Kim Hak-ju. You're under arrest
for murdering Han Eun-young

81
00:09:03,126 --> 00:09:04,962
and attempting to murder Lee Hye-jung.

82
00:09:39,538 --> 00:09:43,125
-You haven't heard from Jae-hee yet?
-No, I'll head over to her right now.

83
00:09:43,208 --> 00:09:44,751
Tell her the ordeal is over.

84
00:09:44,835 --> 00:09:46,378
No more babysitting Yoon Yi-jun.

85
00:09:47,087 --> 00:09:48,046
Yes, sir.

86
00:10:05,731 --> 00:10:08,817
I bet quite a few people had
the wrong idea about you in the military.

87
00:10:09,609 --> 00:10:12,696
Maybe they even asked you out.

88
00:10:12,779 --> 00:10:14,406
We need to go to your hospital.

89
00:10:14,489 --> 00:10:15,699
It's not that serious.

90
00:10:15,782 --> 00:10:17,284
Are you okay, Special Forces?

91
00:10:20,162 --> 00:10:22,998
Give me your name and ID number.

92
00:10:25,584 --> 00:10:28,962
Remember I said I would've fallen for you
if you were a girl?

93
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:34,885
We're both guys.

94
00:10:34,968 --> 00:10:39,097
What if one of us were a man
and one of us were a woman?

95
00:10:40,390 --> 00:10:42,267
Would you have liked me?

96
00:10:47,481 --> 00:10:49,107
Why did you…

97
00:11:18,595 --> 00:11:20,430
I should apologize properly.

98
00:11:31,566 --> 00:11:33,360
-Seok-jin.
-You weren't picking up.

99
00:11:35,153 --> 00:11:36,446
What happened to your face?

100
00:11:41,535 --> 00:11:44,037
I'm glad you managed to
apprehend Kim Hak-ju.

101
00:11:44,579 --> 00:11:45,872
You let him stab you?

102
00:11:47,374 --> 00:11:50,210
-I was wearing a stab proof vest, so--
-How could you say…

103
00:11:58,927 --> 00:12:00,137
Why didn't you dodge it?

104
00:12:03,014 --> 00:12:05,809
We both know you could've dodged it.

105
00:12:09,855 --> 00:12:11,356
He found out I was a woman.

106
00:12:13,692 --> 00:12:15,318
I think I should apologize.

107
00:12:17,028 --> 00:12:19,114
I should still ask for forgiveness.

108
00:12:19,906 --> 00:12:21,074
What comes after that?

109
00:12:21,908 --> 00:12:24,703
Can you reveal
that you're an undercover cop?

110
00:12:25,787 --> 00:12:28,790
We caught the culprit,
so this case will be closed soon.

111
00:12:45,682 --> 00:12:46,850
It's better this way.

112
00:12:46,933 --> 00:12:49,102
You could quit
for being exposed as a woman.

113
00:12:50,770 --> 00:12:54,149
Just like when you went in,
don't leave with any lingering feelings.

114
00:13:00,489 --> 00:13:01,323
Jae-hee.

115
00:13:06,453 --> 00:13:07,662
I care about you a lot.

116
00:13:10,373 --> 00:13:13,835
I care about you and the team a lot.

117
00:13:14,211 --> 00:13:15,378
But not as a colleague.

118
00:13:17,923 --> 00:13:21,510
I hate seeing you risk your life
and pretend to be a man.

119
00:13:24,262 --> 00:13:25,514
I want to be by your side

120
00:13:27,474 --> 00:13:29,142
not as a colleague, but as your man.

121
00:13:33,021 --> 00:13:34,022
Seok-jin, I…

122
00:13:38,568 --> 00:13:39,444
I…

123
00:13:40,987 --> 00:13:42,030
I have feelings for…

124
00:13:47,077 --> 00:13:48,078
I like…

125
00:13:58,380 --> 00:13:59,214
Yoon Yi-jun.

126
00:14:01,466 --> 00:14:04,177
The reason I didn't dodge the knife
was to protect him.

127
00:14:13,019 --> 00:14:14,020
Mr. Yoon.

128
00:14:15,647 --> 00:14:16,731
Sorry, Seok-jin.

129
00:14:21,695 --> 00:14:22,654
Mr. Yoon.

130
00:14:24,614 --> 00:14:25,574
Mr. Yoon.

131
00:14:26,575 --> 00:14:27,576
Mr. Yoon!

132
00:14:42,924 --> 00:14:44,843
I have feelings for…

133
00:14:59,691 --> 00:15:00,650
I like…

134
00:15:28,428 --> 00:15:29,304
Yes, Detective.

135
00:15:30,847 --> 00:15:31,765
Did you catch him?

136
00:15:34,976 --> 00:15:36,144
From the foundation?

137
00:15:36,519 --> 00:15:37,646
Did you find

138
00:15:38,563 --> 00:15:41,441
a recording pen or a dashcam memory card
at the scene?

139
00:15:45,403 --> 00:15:47,906
I understand.
Thank you for your hard work.

140
00:15:59,584 --> 00:16:00,460
What are you doing?

141
00:16:01,211 --> 00:16:02,754
I heard they caught the culprit.

142
00:16:03,713 --> 00:16:06,007
-I should go back home now.
-Already?

143
00:16:06,257 --> 00:16:07,801
I can't live here forever,

144
00:16:08,259 --> 00:16:10,095
mooching off you.

145
00:16:10,679 --> 00:16:12,514
But I just did your laundry.

146
00:16:13,264 --> 00:16:15,433
It'll take a while for your clothes
to be dry.

147
00:16:16,518 --> 00:16:18,353
Look at the woodcutter
stealing my clothes.

148
00:16:18,895 --> 00:16:21,898
I'll let you be the fairy,
so stay one more night. It's the weekend.

149
00:16:22,899 --> 00:16:24,359
People might talk.

150
00:16:25,193 --> 00:16:26,695
Since when did you care?

151
00:16:26,778 --> 00:16:29,864
I'm worrying about your reputation,
not mine.

152
00:16:31,157 --> 00:16:33,159
Who says only women have to be demure?

153
00:16:33,243 --> 00:16:36,496
Men should also behave themselves
if they want to find a good wife.

154
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:47,799
You said you couldn't live there anymore.

155
00:16:48,174 --> 00:16:50,802
You said you were scared of the memories.
I'm scared too.

156
00:16:50,885 --> 00:16:52,429
I'll be moving.

157
00:16:52,512 --> 00:16:54,848
I have an appointment with a realtor,
so I have to go.

158
00:16:55,473 --> 00:16:57,475
-I'll go with you.
-You don't have to.

159
00:16:58,518 --> 00:17:00,937
You said you were meeting Mr. Yoon today.

160
00:17:02,689 --> 00:17:05,233
I have a question, Hye-jung.

161
00:17:12,824 --> 00:17:13,992
What are we?

162
00:17:26,963 --> 00:17:28,006
SPECIAL FORCES

163
00:17:38,475 --> 00:17:39,934
SPECIAL FORCES

164
00:17:50,361 --> 00:17:51,738
Sir, this is Kang Jae-hee.

165
00:17:52,864 --> 00:17:53,990
Please open the door.

166
00:17:55,867 --> 00:17:56,993
Mr. Yoon!

167
00:17:58,203 --> 00:17:59,829
Open the door!

168
00:18:05,794 --> 00:18:07,128
I'm sorry for everything.

169
00:18:08,129 --> 00:18:10,089
Please let me apologize properly.

170
00:18:11,466 --> 00:18:12,550
I'm sorry.

171
00:18:14,010 --> 00:18:15,887
I can explain everything.

172
00:18:15,970 --> 00:18:17,597
It's really sunny outside.

173
00:18:19,307 --> 00:18:21,768
But why does it feel like Siberia in here?

174
00:18:29,192 --> 00:18:30,193
You did it, didn't you?

175
00:18:30,652 --> 00:18:32,487
I'm not in the mood to joke around.

176
00:18:32,570 --> 00:18:35,448
But why are you so prickly today?
Are you a hedgehog?

177
00:18:36,407 --> 00:18:38,451
One, you confessed. Two, you got rejected.

178
00:18:38,535 --> 00:18:40,912
Three, you fired him out of humiliation.

179
00:18:41,704 --> 00:18:43,998
No. One, you confessed.
Two, you got rejected.

180
00:18:44,290 --> 00:18:47,377
Three, you got clingy
and got rejected again?

181
00:18:49,128 --> 00:18:50,547
That didn't happen!

182
00:18:53,550 --> 00:18:56,719
Are you seriously crying? You've lost it.

183
00:18:59,097 --> 00:19:01,975
What happened? Come on, sit down.

184
00:19:02,517 --> 00:19:03,476
Hey.

185
00:19:04,310 --> 00:19:05,687
What's wrong?

186
00:19:05,770 --> 00:19:06,771
How can someone

187
00:19:08,606 --> 00:19:11,234
make me feel so miserable?

188
00:19:11,734 --> 00:19:13,987
Jae-hee likes someone else.

189
00:19:14,070 --> 00:19:15,029
Here.

190
00:19:15,446 --> 00:19:16,322
Secretary Kang does?

191
00:19:16,406 --> 00:19:18,116
Goodness gracious.

192
00:19:20,910 --> 00:19:23,580
Hearing that Jae-hee liked someone else

193
00:19:24,038 --> 00:19:26,958
hurt more than anything
anyone had ever said to me.

194
00:19:27,041 --> 00:19:28,251
I see.

195
00:19:28,334 --> 00:19:30,879
Can you blow your nose first?

196
00:19:32,839 --> 00:19:34,465
Good job.

197
00:19:34,549 --> 00:19:36,175
There, there.

198
00:19:36,259 --> 00:19:37,427
Thanks.

199
00:19:39,470 --> 00:19:40,930
You must've been really sad.

200
00:19:42,515 --> 00:19:43,766
But still,

201
00:19:44,142 --> 00:19:46,227
Jae-hee works here.

202
00:19:46,311 --> 00:19:49,272
You can't let your mood affect
how you treat your employees.

203
00:19:49,355 --> 00:19:53,526
Yes, that's probably why Jae-hee lied.
It was for the money.

204
00:19:54,277 --> 00:19:57,113
In the end,

205
00:19:58,740 --> 00:20:01,618
I was absolutely nothing to Jae-hee.

206
00:20:03,411 --> 00:20:04,579
My gosh.

207
00:20:05,413 --> 00:20:06,789
Here, use this side.

208
00:20:07,624 --> 00:20:08,917
Here you go.

209
00:20:11,628 --> 00:20:13,254
Didn't I use this to blow my nose?

210
00:20:13,671 --> 00:20:15,548
I folded it over to the other side.

211
00:20:18,551 --> 00:20:20,553
KOREA CRIME SCENE INVESTIGATION

212
00:20:30,480 --> 00:20:31,773
Herbicide.

213
00:20:43,201 --> 00:20:45,578
Left-handed. Busted.

214
00:20:47,455 --> 00:20:49,499
Stay quiet all you want.

215
00:20:49,874 --> 00:20:52,251
You're dead meat, Kim Hak-ju.

216
00:20:55,380 --> 00:20:57,674
HAN EUN-YOUNG, LEE HYE-JUNG, PARK MIN-HWAN

217
00:20:59,467 --> 00:21:01,135
What is it now?

218
00:21:01,844 --> 00:21:02,762
You know what?

219
00:21:03,179 --> 00:21:06,432
If something feels off to you,
it feels even worse to me.

220
00:21:06,808 --> 00:21:09,102
Isn't it weird how all this was laid out?

221
00:21:12,021 --> 00:21:14,857
It's as if he's deliberately
making it obvious.

222
00:21:17,694 --> 00:21:18,736
Yes, Captain.

223
00:21:19,904 --> 00:21:21,739
What? Something happened to Kim Hak-ju?

224
00:21:25,910 --> 00:21:27,704
Excuse me. Are you okay?

225
00:21:28,663 --> 00:21:31,290
He collapsed. Call an ambulance now!

226
00:21:33,209 --> 00:21:34,127
He's dead.

227
00:21:39,007 --> 00:21:42,885
Goodness, that's unfortunate.

228
00:21:43,511 --> 00:21:44,971
All right, then.

229
00:21:46,681 --> 00:21:48,933
The evidence is all laid out.

230
00:21:54,564 --> 00:21:58,901
A repeat offender who punished himself
out of guilt for committing murder…

231
00:21:59,402 --> 00:22:00,820
It's a good story, isn't it?

232
00:22:00,903 --> 00:22:03,197
If the pen isn't in evidence,

233
00:22:03,823 --> 00:22:05,992
Managing Director Yoon
will come looking again.

234
00:22:11,456 --> 00:22:14,542
He won't have the time for that.

235
00:22:17,086 --> 00:22:19,338
We'll bury one scandal with another.

236
00:22:19,547 --> 00:22:23,051
CHAIRMAN NA MAN-SEOK

237
00:22:35,563 --> 00:22:37,356
That's insane.

238
00:22:39,108 --> 00:22:40,818
The rumor must have been true.

239
00:22:44,447 --> 00:22:45,782
-Take a look.
-My gosh.

240
00:22:46,074 --> 00:22:47,867
-Is it true?
-It seems so.

241
00:22:48,993 --> 00:22:50,620
It's him, right?

242
00:22:51,621 --> 00:22:54,165
Isn't that the managing director?

243
00:22:54,248 --> 00:22:55,374
Isn't this Mr. Yoon?

244
00:22:58,336 --> 00:23:00,046
-This is Secretary Kang.
-Really?

245
00:23:00,338 --> 00:23:01,964
-They're kissing.
-I knew it.

246
00:23:02,048 --> 00:23:03,674
No wonder they were always together.

247
00:23:04,467 --> 00:23:06,260
I'm afraid I have bad news.

248
00:23:14,060 --> 00:23:15,978
YOON YI-JUN KISSING HIS MALE SECRETARY?

249
00:23:18,981 --> 00:23:20,024
Bring him to me.

250
00:23:20,441 --> 00:23:21,567
Yes, sir.

251
00:23:46,843 --> 00:23:49,554
-We're here on the chairman's orders.
-Mr. Yoon is--

252
00:23:49,637 --> 00:23:51,097
Not him.

253
00:23:51,180 --> 00:23:52,723
He's looking for you.

254
00:23:55,059 --> 00:23:56,727
Chairman Yoon Tae-sik is?

255
00:23:56,811 --> 00:23:58,354
Please turn your phone off.

256
00:23:58,938 --> 00:24:01,107
I won't force it if you cooperate.

257
00:24:10,116 --> 00:24:11,659
Forget damage control for now.

258
00:24:11,742 --> 00:24:13,536
You need to stop the chairman first.

259
00:24:14,036 --> 00:24:16,914
Pull yourself together.
He summoned Secretary Kang.

260
00:24:21,169 --> 00:24:23,629
The chairman made a move himself.

261
00:24:23,713 --> 00:24:25,256
-So what?
-What do you mean?

262
00:24:26,632 --> 00:24:28,009
It's a good thing.

263
00:24:28,092 --> 00:24:30,303
Jae-hee was so upset about the ill rumor.

264
00:24:31,304 --> 00:24:34,348
What better way to clear things up
than to tell my father directly?

265
00:24:35,558 --> 00:24:36,475
Yi-jun.

266
00:24:36,809 --> 00:24:40,897
You understand the situation
better than anyone else.

267
00:24:44,692 --> 00:24:47,820
EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR YOON NA-JUNG

268
00:24:47,904 --> 00:24:50,406
Yoon Yi-jun must be crazy.

269
00:24:51,741 --> 00:24:53,659
He dug his own grave.

270
00:24:58,080 --> 00:25:01,167
The chairman must be absolutely furious
with that temper of his.

271
00:25:01,250 --> 00:25:03,002
I need to go see it for myself.

272
00:25:05,213 --> 00:25:07,673
TAEKANG GROUP
CHAIRMAN'S OFFICE

273
00:25:32,698 --> 00:25:33,824
Move.

274
00:26:05,356 --> 00:26:07,275
It was on the company forum this morning.

275
00:26:07,858 --> 00:26:09,860
You need a company email to access it,

276
00:26:09,944 --> 00:26:11,988
so you probably haven't seen it yet.

277
00:26:21,038 --> 00:26:22,081
By any chance,

278
00:26:22,999 --> 00:26:25,376
did Mr. Yoon figure out you were a woman

279
00:26:26,627 --> 00:26:27,920
at the hospital that day?

280
00:26:30,006 --> 00:26:32,049
How long have you known?

281
00:26:33,843 --> 00:26:37,471
Most men fall for me
when they see me for the first time.

282
00:26:41,726 --> 00:26:43,185
Someone taught me

283
00:26:43,477 --> 00:26:45,604
that silly lines like this actually work.

284
00:26:46,564 --> 00:26:49,191
You seem really tense, Secretary Kang.

285
00:26:52,194 --> 00:26:54,030
Thank you for keeping the secret.

286
00:26:55,323 --> 00:26:57,533
Did you notify Mr. Yoon?

287
00:26:58,159 --> 00:27:00,161
I knew he was on sick leave
after the accident,

288
00:27:00,244 --> 00:27:02,621
but this was too urgent,
so through Attorney Kim.

289
00:27:05,374 --> 00:27:09,170
He lost the recording pen,
his plan fell apart,

290
00:27:10,588 --> 00:27:13,758
and he was betrayed
by the person he likes.

291
00:27:14,550 --> 00:27:16,177
He must be a mess inside.

292
00:27:18,554 --> 00:27:20,973
If it were me,
I would've ignored it out of spite.

293
00:27:21,057 --> 00:27:22,683
But Mr. Yoon came rushing over here.

294
00:27:29,523 --> 00:27:32,401
You must be hellbent on
running this company into the ground.

295
00:27:36,155 --> 00:27:37,323
Explain.

296
00:27:38,532 --> 00:27:39,950
It's just as you see it.

297
00:27:40,034 --> 00:27:41,494
Do you hear him, Father?

298
00:27:41,952 --> 00:27:44,038
He's gone insane.

299
00:27:44,121 --> 00:27:45,623
I'm the only one who likes him.

300
00:27:46,123 --> 00:27:47,083
That photo too.

301
00:27:47,666 --> 00:27:50,252
I forced him when he didn't want it,
so don't blame him.

302
00:27:51,170 --> 00:27:54,090
If you're going to anyway,
make sure he's well compensated for it.

303
00:27:54,173 --> 00:27:55,674
How dare you?

304
00:28:01,722 --> 00:28:02,765
You won't apologize?

305
00:28:13,109 --> 00:28:14,276
The two of you, get out.

306
00:28:16,070 --> 00:28:18,197
Why me, Father?

307
00:28:18,280 --> 00:28:19,365
Get out!

308
00:28:29,667 --> 00:28:31,085
Who do you think you are?

309
00:28:32,044 --> 00:28:33,629
What's wrong with you?

310
00:28:34,922 --> 00:28:38,008
I let you get away with your antics,
but you've completely lost it.

311
00:28:38,092 --> 00:28:40,302
Do you have any idea
how much this will cost us?

312
00:28:40,386 --> 00:28:42,430
That's why I'm here to clean up the mess.

313
00:28:44,181 --> 00:28:45,433
Tell me what you want.

314
00:28:46,142 --> 00:28:47,810
It's not like I don't know you.

315
00:28:49,520 --> 00:28:51,397
I told them to pick an auspicious date.

316
00:28:53,524 --> 00:28:54,525
An auspicious date?

317
00:28:55,192 --> 00:28:58,320
I heard there would be an event
at Director Lee's art center.

318
00:29:00,322 --> 00:29:03,742
No need to set another date.
Attend it and announce the marriage.

319
00:29:07,830 --> 00:29:09,498
What happens to that innocent kid

320
00:29:10,416 --> 00:29:11,709
depends on how you behave.

321
00:29:22,386 --> 00:29:23,345
Mr. Yoon.

322
00:29:27,433 --> 00:29:28,809
Sir, let's talk.

323
00:29:29,894 --> 00:29:32,605
I know you're mad.
I get that you're disappointed.

324
00:29:34,315 --> 00:29:35,566
I don't want to hear it.

325
00:29:39,904 --> 00:29:42,364
I've always been mistaken for a man.

326
00:29:44,200 --> 00:29:46,076
At first, I didn't think much of it.

327
00:29:47,578 --> 00:29:49,497
I didn't feel guilty either.

328
00:29:49,580 --> 00:29:53,042
But as time went on, I regretted it.

329
00:29:54,126 --> 00:29:55,127
I was scared.

330
00:29:58,005 --> 00:30:00,591
I knew it was the right thing to do
to tell you the truth.

331
00:30:02,968 --> 00:30:05,054
But I thought it all would end
if I told you.

332
00:30:07,056 --> 00:30:09,558
That's why I kept putting it off.

333
00:30:15,189 --> 00:30:17,233
The real reason why I deceived you is--

334
00:30:17,316 --> 00:30:19,235
You should've told me

335
00:30:21,445 --> 00:30:23,489
when you realized how I felt about you.

336
00:30:28,160 --> 00:30:29,787
You should've told me

337
00:30:31,455 --> 00:30:33,249
when I confessed to you.

338
00:30:37,002 --> 00:30:38,003
I'm sorry.

339
00:30:39,964 --> 00:30:41,173
I was a coward.

340
00:30:44,635 --> 00:30:45,511
Yes.

341
00:30:46,971 --> 00:30:48,138
You were a coward.

342
00:30:51,267 --> 00:30:52,184
Forget it.

343
00:30:53,352 --> 00:30:57,064
Blaming you after all this time
won't change anything.

344
00:31:01,485 --> 00:31:03,237
You should've shown some respect

345
00:31:05,489 --> 00:31:07,449
to the man who said he liked you.

346
00:31:15,249 --> 00:31:16,375
Let's end it here.

347
00:31:30,931 --> 00:31:31,807
LEE SI-A

348
00:31:35,352 --> 00:31:38,022
I see the chairman sent me
a precious gift.

349
00:31:43,027 --> 00:31:44,903
You set the wedding date.

350
00:31:47,573 --> 00:31:49,033
How can I ever thank him?

351
00:31:49,366 --> 00:31:51,869
I should give the chairman
a little something in return.

352
00:31:51,952 --> 00:31:55,164
Save me a seat for the opening day.

353
00:31:55,706 --> 00:31:57,333
You're always welcome to come.

354
00:31:58,334 --> 00:32:02,046
But why do you sound so upset
when you have such an auspicious date?

355
00:32:03,839 --> 00:32:05,090
Well,

356
00:32:06,008 --> 00:32:10,471
I guess love is hard,
and the truth always hurts.

357
00:32:22,274 --> 00:32:23,192
Sir…

358
00:32:41,710 --> 00:32:43,754
Did you pin me to the wall to be romantic?

359
00:32:43,837 --> 00:32:45,673
This isn't the time for butterflies.

360
00:32:45,756 --> 00:32:47,675
Why? I want butterflies.

361
00:32:50,427 --> 00:32:51,595
Why didn't you tell me

362
00:32:52,304 --> 00:32:53,972
you lost the recording pen on purpose?

363
00:32:56,558 --> 00:32:59,728
Right, I need to review the papers
before sending them to audit.

364
00:33:01,605 --> 00:33:04,358
Explain, clarify, make excuses,
and scream.

365
00:33:06,819 --> 00:33:08,278
-Scream?
-If I find that

366
00:33:08,362 --> 00:33:11,657
the first three don't give me an answer,
I'll make you scream.

367
00:33:13,200 --> 00:33:14,201
How did you know?

368
00:33:20,290 --> 00:33:21,458
So I'm right.

369
00:33:22,292 --> 00:33:24,378
For losing something so crucial,

370
00:33:24,461 --> 00:33:27,256
you, Mr. Yoon, and Secretary Kang
seemed just too calm,

371
00:33:27,673 --> 00:33:29,466
so I tested you.

372
00:33:39,268 --> 00:33:42,062
Trying to straighten a bull's horns

373
00:33:43,313 --> 00:33:46,233
only ends up killing the bull.

374
00:33:48,736 --> 00:33:51,155
How could my clever nephew not know that?

375
00:33:59,663 --> 00:34:02,499
I went through
the confidential documents you gave me.

376
00:34:02,583 --> 00:34:05,419
I checked the FS
and the projected adjustment reports,

377
00:34:05,502 --> 00:34:07,212
but nothing looked suspicious.

378
00:34:08,338 --> 00:34:11,008
Scrap them.
Look into the Taekang Cultural Foundation.

379
00:34:11,091 --> 00:34:11,967
The foundation?

380
00:34:12,050 --> 00:34:16,221
It's been about ten years
since my father put my uncle in charge.

381
00:34:16,305 --> 00:34:19,057
Chief Secretary Na Man-seok
should be listed as a chairman.

382
00:34:19,141 --> 00:34:21,769
But the size of Taekang Foundation…

383
00:34:21,852 --> 00:34:22,811
Right.

384
00:34:22,895 --> 00:34:25,773
The foundation runs
a prisoner rehabilitation program.

385
00:34:25,856 --> 00:34:26,774
Are you saying

386
00:34:27,232 --> 00:34:29,693
the prisoners' accounts were used
under borrowed names

387
00:34:29,777 --> 00:34:32,154
to move the company's retained earnings?

388
00:34:33,030 --> 00:34:34,990
Dig into everything
related to that program.

389
00:34:35,991 --> 00:34:37,201
You'll find something.

390
00:34:37,534 --> 00:34:38,535
Yes, sir.

391
00:34:39,536 --> 00:34:42,706
But how did you know
it was the Taekang Cultural Foundation?

392
00:34:53,300 --> 00:34:55,385
HONAM RESTAURANT

393
00:34:58,514 --> 00:35:01,016
Good work. You fought so hard for this.

394
00:35:02,851 --> 00:35:04,770
You were pretty much
the one who caught him.

395
00:35:09,149 --> 00:35:10,442
FOUR DAYS BEFORE THE MEMORIAL

396
00:35:10,526 --> 00:35:12,945
Captain. On Mr. Yoon's orders,

397
00:35:13,028 --> 00:35:17,157
we linked the pen's location
to his phone and our tablet.

398
00:35:21,036 --> 00:35:24,706
He wants to see where the pen will end up.

399
00:35:24,998 --> 00:35:28,627
Na Man-seok and Yoon Na-jung
won't just sit back. Will you be okay?

400
00:35:30,003 --> 00:35:32,798
Wear a stab vest for the time being
in case something happens.

401
00:35:32,881 --> 00:35:33,799
Yes, sir.

402
00:35:34,341 --> 00:35:35,342
This time,

403
00:35:36,802 --> 00:35:38,428
I won't let that bastard get away.

404
00:35:42,140 --> 00:35:43,100
It's nothing, sir.

405
00:35:44,434 --> 00:35:47,145
Let's finish the investigation
before this weekend.

406
00:35:48,897 --> 00:35:49,857
This weekend?

407
00:35:49,940 --> 00:35:52,192
Kim Hak-ju died in custody.

408
00:35:52,276 --> 00:35:53,694
We could end up taking the fall.

409
00:35:53,777 --> 00:35:56,154
Kim Hak-ju isn't the real target.

410
00:35:56,488 --> 00:35:58,156
He's clearly their scapegoat.

411
00:35:58,240 --> 00:36:01,952
We only agreed to catch the killer,
so we'll transfer the rest.

412
00:36:02,035 --> 00:36:04,913
We also confirmed the pen ended up
with Na Man-seok.

413
00:36:04,997 --> 00:36:07,708
We need to dig into Na Man-seok, Captain.

414
00:36:15,549 --> 00:36:17,175
How could you give him your heart?

415
00:36:22,347 --> 00:36:24,349
You gave the most dangerous one
of all things.

416
00:36:27,311 --> 00:36:28,312
I know.

417
00:36:30,105 --> 00:36:31,440
I know I shouldn't have.

418
00:36:31,523 --> 00:36:32,733
Then end it now.

419
00:36:33,483 --> 00:36:35,402
You would know best why you have to.

420
00:36:36,194 --> 00:36:37,654
Including Kim Hak-ju's death,

421
00:36:37,738 --> 00:36:39,823
this entire case isn't
something we can handle.

422
00:36:42,659 --> 00:36:44,661
Wrap it up
without letting Yoon Yi-jun catch on

423
00:36:44,745 --> 00:36:46,288
before the autopsy results come in.

424
00:37:03,013 --> 00:37:04,765
Kang Jae-hee…

425
00:37:07,225 --> 00:37:08,310
Turns out she's a girl.

426
00:37:09,937 --> 00:37:11,730
Did you keep quiet despite knowing it?

427
00:37:11,813 --> 00:37:13,315
Secretary Kang is a girl?

428
00:37:14,024 --> 00:37:14,942
Oh my.

429
00:37:15,943 --> 00:37:16,985
My gosh.

430
00:37:17,069 --> 00:37:21,114
I had no idea, Ms. Yoon.

431
00:37:21,198 --> 00:37:24,868
What? She really fooled everyone.

432
00:37:26,078 --> 00:37:28,163
Did she pretend to be a man for the money?

433
00:37:28,246 --> 00:37:31,959
Then she should've accepted my offer,
just like you did, right?

434
00:37:35,921 --> 00:37:37,089
Ms. Yoon.

435
00:37:37,172 --> 00:37:40,300
Kang Jae-hee.

436
00:37:40,884 --> 00:37:43,095
I feel like there's something more to her.

437
00:37:43,679 --> 00:37:45,847
-A detective…
-Right.

438
00:37:47,724 --> 00:37:50,102
I heard that gardener or whatever died.

439
00:37:54,189 --> 00:37:55,232
Are you scared?

440
00:37:58,360 --> 00:38:00,112
Who cares if the police know?

441
00:38:00,195 --> 00:38:02,280
You simply passed on information.

442
00:38:02,698 --> 00:38:05,993
You'll get a couple of years
if Yoon Yi-jun sues you.

443
00:38:09,246 --> 00:38:10,706
Call me when you are released.

444
00:38:14,876 --> 00:38:17,004
-Hye-jung.
-You hid it from me.

445
00:38:17,087 --> 00:38:18,630
That means you didn't trust me.

446
00:38:19,881 --> 00:38:23,510
It's because
I was trying to keep you safe.

447
00:38:24,803 --> 00:38:26,930
Why do you get to decide that for me?

448
00:38:27,305 --> 00:38:29,016
Why shouldn't I?

449
00:38:29,349 --> 00:38:33,270
So I should be grateful
for any information you choose to tell me?

450
00:38:33,353 --> 00:38:35,188
That's not what I meant.

451
00:38:35,689 --> 00:38:37,524
You asked me what we are to each other.

452
00:38:38,442 --> 00:38:39,651
We can't trust each other.

453
00:38:40,652 --> 00:38:41,653
We never will.

454
00:38:42,112 --> 00:38:43,905
What was I supposed to do? I was worried!

455
00:38:43,989 --> 00:38:47,784
I'm terrified that you'll put yourself
in danger by knowing too much!

456
00:38:52,956 --> 00:38:56,084
-Answer the phone.
-You don't give a damn why I did it.

457
00:38:56,168 --> 00:38:59,004
-Who cares about a phone call?
-Answer the phone!

458
00:38:59,087 --> 00:39:00,630
What if it's an important call?

459
00:39:01,339 --> 00:39:02,299
Stay right there.

460
00:39:06,011 --> 00:39:07,512
If it's not urgent, call me--

461
00:39:10,974 --> 00:39:12,392
The dashcam backup footage?

462
00:39:14,686 --> 00:39:15,562
Okay.

463
00:39:24,946 --> 00:39:26,323
You seem carefree.

464
00:39:29,076 --> 00:39:30,327
What will you do about it?

465
00:39:30,744 --> 00:39:33,997
I'm about to get dumped by Hye-jung
because of that GPS.

466
00:39:35,123 --> 00:39:36,625
Don't complain.

467
00:39:41,046 --> 00:39:42,506
She hasn't dumped you yet.

468
00:39:42,964 --> 00:39:44,925
And you were already dumped,

469
00:39:45,008 --> 00:39:47,094
slapped hard by the chairman,

470
00:39:47,177 --> 00:39:48,845
and are being sold off to get married,

471
00:39:48,929 --> 00:39:51,431
so you must be jealous of me, aren't you?

472
00:39:55,811 --> 00:39:58,688
You really can't get over Jae-hee?

473
00:39:59,356 --> 00:40:01,858
Then stop moping around
and do what you're good at.

474
00:40:01,942 --> 00:40:03,401
And what is that?

475
00:40:03,944 --> 00:40:06,738
The man they call a ruthless strategist
and a thug in M&A.

476
00:40:06,822 --> 00:40:07,823
Don't be humble.

477
00:40:09,241 --> 00:40:11,284
I don't like taking things by force.

478
00:40:12,244 --> 00:40:14,830
Is that so?
You don't like it when it's forced?

479
00:40:15,288 --> 00:40:18,041
You want Jae-hee to love you
of his own free will?

480
00:40:25,257 --> 00:40:26,216
I'm the one

481
00:40:27,425 --> 00:40:28,510
who was driving.

482
00:40:32,472 --> 00:40:34,641
The brake didn't work,

483
00:40:35,559 --> 00:40:37,352
and the car was coming straight at us.

484
00:40:39,187 --> 00:40:41,898
Before I knew it, I'd swerved the wheel.

485
00:40:43,900 --> 00:40:45,318
I didn't care if I got hurt.

486
00:40:47,154 --> 00:40:50,157
All I could think about was making sure
Jae-hee was safe.

487
00:40:52,742 --> 00:40:55,912
I don't understand
why I like Jae-hee so much.

488
00:41:00,333 --> 00:41:02,294
I want to demand to know

489
00:41:04,546 --> 00:41:06,590
why Jae-hee did that to me

490
00:41:07,757 --> 00:41:09,384
and why Jae-hee can't like me.

491
00:41:09,843 --> 00:41:11,887
But I can't even do that.

492
00:41:13,555 --> 00:41:15,056
I'm terrified of being rejected.

493
00:41:18,059 --> 00:41:18,935
You know what?

494
00:41:21,646 --> 00:41:23,565
If I could buy it with money,

495
00:41:25,066 --> 00:41:26,818
I would've given everything I had

496
00:41:28,236 --> 00:41:29,321
to buy Jae-hee's love.

497
00:41:31,072 --> 00:41:32,240
Now you have someone

498
00:41:34,451 --> 00:41:36,786
who you cherish more than yourself.

499
00:41:39,623 --> 00:41:41,374
I'm not sure if this helps, but…

500
00:41:42,083 --> 00:41:44,544
"How much? How much will it take?"

501
00:41:45,128 --> 00:41:47,464
Even Won Bin couldn't buy it.

502
00:41:49,549 --> 00:41:50,717
Gosh.

503
00:41:51,593 --> 00:41:53,136
This is too painful to watch.

504
00:41:56,348 --> 00:41:58,934
Hey, don't cry again after watching this.

505
00:41:59,601 --> 00:42:01,102
You were a snotty mess last time.

506
00:42:02,520 --> 00:42:03,355
Here.

507
00:42:07,484 --> 00:42:09,527
I requested the backup footage that day,

508
00:42:09,861 --> 00:42:12,739
-hoping to catch the culprit's face.
-You must be the real culprit.

509
00:42:13,281 --> 00:42:14,491
He's under my protection.

510
00:42:16,159 --> 00:42:18,787
In the meantime,
the police managed to catch the culprit.

511
00:42:19,287 --> 00:42:23,041
So I forgot about it, but they sent over
what was backed up on the cloud today.

512
00:42:27,087 --> 00:42:28,797
I won't let you.

513
00:42:38,723 --> 00:42:41,268
How can he let him stab…

514
00:42:41,351 --> 00:42:43,144
Go ask people on the street

515
00:42:43,478 --> 00:42:45,146
if they'd take a knife for their boss.

516
00:42:45,647 --> 00:42:48,525
Most would ask
if they could stab their boss instead.

517
00:42:50,652 --> 00:42:52,112
You don't need to buy his heart.

518
00:43:00,120 --> 00:43:01,913
Yoon Yi-jun will get married,

519
00:43:02,998 --> 00:43:04,332
and I'll pull out.

520
00:43:06,459 --> 00:43:08,211
That's the right thing to do.

521
00:43:09,170 --> 00:43:10,338
It is.

522
00:43:17,220 --> 00:43:19,180
I don't even want to talk about it.

523
00:43:19,264 --> 00:43:21,933
A tomboy came out of nowhere
in the middle of the night,

524
00:43:22,600 --> 00:43:23,935
and I was so startled.

525
00:43:24,269 --> 00:43:27,314
Kids these days do whatever they want.

526
00:43:27,397 --> 00:43:29,691
Why don't you set her up with her son?

527
00:43:29,774 --> 00:43:30,942
They're of marrying age.

528
00:43:31,026 --> 00:43:32,694
Don't even say that.

529
00:43:32,777 --> 00:43:34,696
Gi-chan has a girlfriend.

530
00:43:35,030 --> 00:43:36,865
She goes to Taekang with him.

531
00:43:37,866 --> 00:43:40,702
I'll have Jae-hee marry
a public servant like her.

532
00:43:41,077 --> 00:43:45,206
They'll both receive a hefty sum
for their retirement.

533
00:43:45,290 --> 00:43:46,166
Mom.

534
00:43:55,717 --> 00:43:58,219
She mentions Taekang every chance she has.

535
00:43:59,554 --> 00:44:01,931
Acting like her son is hot stuff.

536
00:44:02,015 --> 00:44:04,601
Who cares if he works at Taekang?

537
00:44:04,684 --> 00:44:07,645
Bring me Taekang's heir.
Let's see if I even bat an eye!

538
00:44:08,813 --> 00:44:12,567
Are you the only one in Korea
who has to catch all the bad guys?

539
00:44:12,942 --> 00:44:15,111
What's wrong with your face?

540
00:44:15,737 --> 00:44:17,530
Are you hurt anywhere else?

541
00:44:17,614 --> 00:44:18,698
I'm fine.

542
00:44:19,783 --> 00:44:20,617
Where's Dad?

543
00:44:22,869 --> 00:44:24,496
EXPERT ON ROMANCE

544
00:44:24,579 --> 00:44:26,498
Take a nice, warm shower.

545
00:44:27,290 --> 00:44:29,000
Then pamper your skin

546
00:44:30,502 --> 00:44:32,128
with your favorite face mask.

547
00:44:32,420 --> 00:44:33,963
Moisturizing.

548
00:44:34,047 --> 00:44:36,674
You have to keep your skin hydrated.

549
00:44:36,758 --> 00:44:38,718
Finally, while reading a book
that you enjoy,

550
00:44:40,303 --> 00:44:41,638
you fall into a deep sleep.

551
00:44:42,722 --> 00:44:43,848
Good night, everyone.

552
00:44:53,024 --> 00:44:54,859
-Who is it?
-Bonjour.

553
00:44:55,610 --> 00:44:56,528
Dad?

554
00:44:58,780 --> 00:45:00,824
Princess. You're still up?

555
00:45:00,907 --> 00:45:02,075
-Yes.
-I see.

556
00:45:02,367 --> 00:45:03,201
Can I come in?

557
00:45:04,452 --> 00:45:05,286
Sure.

558
00:45:05,745 --> 00:45:06,788
Craft beer?

559
00:45:07,914 --> 00:45:10,250
You got the expensive stuff.

560
00:45:10,750 --> 00:45:12,252
I tapped into my slush fund.

561
00:45:12,710 --> 00:45:14,045
Don't tell your mom.

562
00:45:14,129 --> 00:45:15,547
I'm going to tell her.

563
00:45:15,630 --> 00:45:17,132
Where's my phone?

564
00:45:17,674 --> 00:45:18,508
Hey.

565
00:45:19,634 --> 00:45:21,136
Gosh, you cheeky brat.

566
00:45:21,761 --> 00:45:23,263
I can snitch too, you know.

567
00:45:23,346 --> 00:45:25,849
-What?
-That you're doing this

568
00:45:26,307 --> 00:45:30,145
because of your boss
who's got money and a decent face.

569
00:45:30,728 --> 00:45:32,439
-Hey.
-How did you know?

570
00:45:32,522 --> 00:45:33,857
Tell me his name.

571
00:45:34,232 --> 00:45:36,568
How dare he do that to my daughter,
my pride and joy?

572
00:45:37,569 --> 00:45:38,736
How dare he reject you?

573
00:45:39,404 --> 00:45:41,781
No, that's not it.
Why would I get rejected?

574
00:45:42,323 --> 00:45:43,158
You didn't?

575
00:45:44,200 --> 00:45:46,119
Then why are you sulking?

576
00:45:48,538 --> 00:45:49,539
He's getting married.

577
00:45:52,417 --> 00:45:53,251
Jae-hee.

578
00:45:54,210 --> 00:45:55,587
That's called getting rejected.

579
00:45:55,962 --> 00:45:57,088
Is it?

580
00:45:57,589 --> 00:46:00,967
But that jerk is getting married
to another girl?

581
00:46:02,760 --> 00:46:06,514
I'll make a video of him
so everyone knows how awful he is.

582
00:46:06,598 --> 00:46:09,726
Wait, this is to get more viewership,
isn't it?

583
00:46:09,809 --> 00:46:13,855
Not at all.
I don't really care about viewership.

584
00:46:13,938 --> 00:46:16,274
What kind of dad
exploits his daughter's heartbreak?

585
00:46:17,400 --> 00:46:19,819
Anyway, forget about
a crappy guy like him.

586
00:46:20,320 --> 00:46:21,654
He's not worth your time.

587
00:46:24,657 --> 00:46:26,868
I just feel bad.

588
00:46:27,577 --> 00:46:31,206
He got blamed for things he didn't do,
became the subject of gossip,

589
00:46:32,665 --> 00:46:34,000
and even got slapped.

590
00:46:35,418 --> 00:46:37,378
I couldn't even tell him I like him.

591
00:46:41,341 --> 00:46:42,217
Jae-hee.

592
00:46:43,051 --> 00:46:46,471
There are things in life
you should never leave unfinished.

593
00:46:47,305 --> 00:46:48,181
What is it?

594
00:46:49,516 --> 00:46:50,433
Food

595
00:46:51,684 --> 00:46:52,685
and regrets.

596
00:46:55,396 --> 00:46:56,940
You only live once.

597
00:46:57,732 --> 00:47:00,485
You have Kang Seok-gu and Cho Suk-ja
behind you.

598
00:47:01,152 --> 00:47:04,531
So just this once, follow your heart.

599
00:47:05,365 --> 00:47:06,824
I'll take care of everything.

600
00:47:09,160 --> 00:47:10,787
-I'm cool, aren't I?
-Yes.

601
00:47:16,334 --> 00:47:19,379
-You're going to film that, aren't you?
-Not at all.

602
00:47:19,462 --> 00:47:22,048
-Come on.
-It's good content.

603
00:47:22,131 --> 00:47:24,384
-If it's okay with you…
-Is that all you care about?

604
00:47:24,842 --> 00:47:26,261
-Wait.
-I almost cried.

605
00:47:26,344 --> 00:47:29,138
-Just go home. Go!
-Hey.

606
00:47:29,222 --> 00:47:30,932
Leave!

607
00:47:32,392 --> 00:47:36,563
SEVEN WINTERS
ARTIST KO'S SPECIAL EXHIBITION, PROPOSAL

608
00:47:36,646 --> 00:47:39,315
WISHING THE BEST FOR THE EXHIBITION

609
00:47:39,399 --> 00:47:42,569
DIRECTION TO THE PRESS CONFERENCE

610
00:47:57,792 --> 00:47:59,377
This is on the chairman's orders.

611
00:47:59,460 --> 00:48:01,754
I'm sorry to have to tell you this,
Secretary Kang.

612
00:48:02,338 --> 00:48:05,174
As of today, your employment
as Yoon Yi-jun's personal secretary

613
00:48:06,134 --> 00:48:07,385
is terminated.

614
00:48:10,430 --> 00:48:11,723
I knew this was coming.

615
00:48:13,016 --> 00:48:13,850
Attorney Kim.

616
00:48:15,184 --> 00:48:16,769
I have a favor.

617
00:48:16,853 --> 00:48:19,606
Yes, anything for you, sir.

618
00:48:19,897 --> 00:48:20,898
-What?
-What?

619
00:48:21,274 --> 00:48:23,234
-What did--
-How did you get good at fighting?

620
00:48:23,318 --> 00:48:24,527
-What?
-What?

621
00:48:25,028 --> 00:48:26,195
The dashcam…

622
00:48:26,946 --> 00:48:28,281
Never mind.

623
00:48:28,698 --> 00:48:29,616
Anyway, go ahead.

624
00:48:31,117 --> 00:48:33,036
Please help me meet Mr. Yoon.

625
00:48:33,911 --> 00:48:35,580
I have something I have to tell him.

626
00:48:36,623 --> 00:48:38,666
But he's been avoiding me since we met.

627
00:48:40,168 --> 00:48:41,377
Where is he?

628
00:48:41,711 --> 00:48:42,879
The thing is…

629
00:48:46,132 --> 00:48:47,467
REAL ESTATE GIFT AGREEMENT

630
00:48:47,550 --> 00:48:49,052
PRENUPTIAL AGREEMENT

631
00:48:49,135 --> 00:48:50,470
According to my lawyer,

632
00:48:50,553 --> 00:48:52,889
this is what both parties agreed on.

633
00:48:52,972 --> 00:48:55,808
We'll each keep a copy,
and they'll notarize them separately.

634
00:48:56,351 --> 00:48:57,310
So read it carefully.

635
00:49:04,609 --> 00:49:05,568
SIGNATURE

636
00:49:13,993 --> 00:49:15,078
That was today?

637
00:49:16,663 --> 00:49:19,832
I guess that's what the superrich do.

638
00:49:21,125 --> 00:49:23,544
I thought there was still time
until the wedding.

639
00:49:24,003 --> 00:49:24,921
You know,

640
00:49:25,922 --> 00:49:26,964
I'm not one to meddle.

641
00:49:27,340 --> 00:49:29,425
But watching you two is driving me crazy.

642
00:49:29,509 --> 00:49:31,135
Why do you keep going back and forth?

643
00:49:31,427 --> 00:49:33,346
He's smart,
so you think he's good at dating.

644
00:49:33,429 --> 00:49:35,973
No! He's a total fool
when it comes to love.

645
00:49:36,057 --> 00:49:37,350
I hear you like someone else.

646
00:49:37,934 --> 00:49:39,185
I heard you even confessed.

647
00:49:39,268 --> 00:49:41,354
So why are you still pining like this?

648
00:49:41,437 --> 00:49:43,523
-Even that dashcam footage--
-Wait.

649
00:49:44,232 --> 00:49:46,609
I confessed? To whom?

650
00:49:46,693 --> 00:49:48,319
I heard you confessed!

651
00:49:48,403 --> 00:49:50,655
I saw him cry his eyes…

652
00:49:50,738 --> 00:49:53,116
I have feelings for…

653
00:49:58,037 --> 00:49:58,955
I like…

654
00:50:02,083 --> 00:50:03,126
How much did he hear?

655
00:50:03,209 --> 00:50:05,420
What do you mean? I don't know about that.

656
00:50:05,503 --> 00:50:07,422
But your mixed signals are destroying

657
00:50:07,505 --> 00:50:09,424
-his soul, and--
-Stop.

658
00:50:09,716 --> 00:50:11,426
So he's at the art center?

659
00:50:16,848 --> 00:50:17,682
Are you mad?

660
00:50:18,015 --> 00:50:21,144
Give me the key. I'll drive.

661
00:50:28,693 --> 00:50:30,278
There's a car!

662
00:50:30,361 --> 00:50:32,530
-Secretary Kang, I mean, Jae-hee!
-Brace yourself.

663
00:50:36,701 --> 00:50:39,912
You should've talked to him sooner!
Why did you let him misunderstand?

664
00:50:39,996 --> 00:50:43,541
How could I tell him when he never asked?
He wouldn't even see me!

665
00:50:43,624 --> 00:50:47,003
That idiot only has eyes for you.
It's obvious when he acts all cold!

666
00:50:47,086 --> 00:50:50,715
I thought that was because I deceived him.

667
00:50:50,798 --> 00:50:53,509
What do you mean?
What could you possibly have done?

668
00:50:55,178 --> 00:50:56,804
I guess he didn't tell you.

669
00:50:56,888 --> 00:50:57,805
What is it?

670
00:50:57,889 --> 00:51:00,308
Mr. Yoon and even Secretary Lee know.

671
00:51:00,391 --> 00:51:04,020
What do they both know that I don't?

672
00:51:05,730 --> 00:51:08,065
-I'm a woman.
-Are you kidding me?

673
00:51:08,149 --> 00:51:09,317
The Adam's apple--

674
00:51:10,860 --> 00:51:11,903
You don't have one.

675
00:51:11,986 --> 00:51:13,988
Yes, you're right.

676
00:51:14,071 --> 00:51:16,741
I have XX chromosomes and no Adam's apple.

677
00:51:18,117 --> 00:51:20,953
I'm biologically female.

678
00:51:21,579 --> 00:51:22,413
For real?

679
00:51:24,415 --> 00:51:25,374
Really, ma'am?

680
00:51:31,422 --> 00:51:33,674
The article has been published, sir.

681
00:51:34,550 --> 00:51:35,551
What about Yi-jun?

682
00:51:35,968 --> 00:51:38,304
He signed the contract.

683
00:51:43,976 --> 00:51:47,438
I guess they're all here to visit
the daughter of the future president.

684
00:51:52,485 --> 00:51:54,862
Director Lee Si-a's marriage news
officially dropped.

685
00:51:54,946 --> 00:51:58,407
"Taekang Chairman Yoon's youngest son,
Yoon Yi-jun, to marry in October."

686
00:51:59,367 --> 00:52:00,868
Over there!

687
00:52:00,952 --> 00:52:02,203
-Here!
-Sir.

688
00:52:03,538 --> 00:52:04,789
-Please stay back.
-Sir.

689
00:52:04,872 --> 00:52:06,207
-Is it true?
-A comment?

690
00:52:06,290 --> 00:52:07,792
-Please say a word!
-Is it true?

691
00:52:17,969 --> 00:52:19,428
That felt like an F1 simulator.

692
00:52:19,804 --> 00:52:20,763
You can't go inside!

693
00:52:22,598 --> 00:52:23,641
You can't enter.

694
00:52:23,933 --> 00:52:24,892
She's a friend.

695
00:52:25,393 --> 00:52:26,936
Yes, sir.

696
00:52:27,770 --> 00:52:28,646
Please go in.

697
00:52:31,023 --> 00:52:32,066
Thank you.

698
00:52:32,149 --> 00:52:33,442
I've heard a lot about you.

699
00:53:00,219 --> 00:53:02,763
The press conference will start
in 30 minutes--

700
00:53:02,847 --> 00:53:05,182
Congratulations on your marriage.
When is the wedding?

701
00:53:05,266 --> 00:53:07,268
The wedding announcement just went public.

702
00:53:07,351 --> 00:53:10,021
Is your attendance today
a show of support?

703
00:53:10,104 --> 00:53:12,940
Could this be an announcement
aimed at the presidential election?

704
00:53:13,024 --> 00:53:15,234
Where will the wedding take place?

705
00:53:15,318 --> 00:53:17,695
Will it be at Taekang Hotel?

706
00:53:17,778 --> 00:53:19,030
Please say a word.

707
00:53:39,926 --> 00:53:42,345
The wedding announcement is false.

708
00:53:42,428 --> 00:53:43,512
-What?
-False?

709
00:53:49,060 --> 00:53:52,605
We just broke off our engagement.

710
00:53:54,732 --> 00:53:57,109
Broke off your engagement?
What's the reason?

711
00:53:57,944 --> 00:54:02,114
Recently, photos of you and your secretary
made headlines.

712
00:54:02,198 --> 00:54:03,616
You kissed your male secretary.

713
00:54:03,699 --> 00:54:06,327
What is your relationship with him?
Are you dating him?

714
00:54:06,410 --> 00:54:08,621
-Are the photos real?
-Are you coming out as gay?

715
00:54:08,704 --> 00:54:09,705
Please explain.

716
00:54:09,789 --> 00:54:12,208
Please explain
why you broke off the engagement.

717
00:54:12,917 --> 00:54:14,251
That photo made headlines?

718
00:54:14,335 --> 00:54:17,088
Let's start by asking
how you got hold of them.

719
00:54:17,922 --> 00:54:20,299
Next, our relationship is
that of a boss and secretary.

720
00:54:20,383 --> 00:54:24,095
Next question. The photo is real.
And I like the person. Next.

721
00:54:24,845 --> 00:54:27,807
Whether I am gay or not
depends on the gender of the person

722
00:54:29,058 --> 00:54:29,976
whom I like.

723
00:54:39,819 --> 00:54:40,903
This is the end.

724
00:54:41,654 --> 00:54:43,280
MARRIAGE TERMINATION AGREEMENT

725
00:54:46,409 --> 00:54:48,536
You're free now. What's the plan?

726
00:54:50,371 --> 00:54:52,206
Now that everything's settled,

727
00:54:52,665 --> 00:54:54,000
I have to go after her.

728
00:54:55,001 --> 00:54:56,293
How understanding of you.

729
00:54:56,377 --> 00:54:58,254
What do you see
in a woman who deceived you?

730
00:54:58,337 --> 00:54:59,755
She saved my life.

731
00:55:00,297 --> 00:55:03,175
I've always been understanding toward her.

732
00:55:03,968 --> 00:55:05,052
What if she rejects you?

733
00:55:05,553 --> 00:55:06,512
I'll wait.

734
00:55:08,180 --> 00:55:10,016
I'll pray every day

735
00:55:10,433 --> 00:55:12,184
for her to break up with that guy.

736
00:55:13,310 --> 00:55:16,772
I think Chairman Yoon
will be reaching for his golf club soon.

737
00:55:17,815 --> 00:55:18,774
Who knows?

738
00:55:19,734 --> 00:55:21,444
It'll work out somehow.

739
00:55:24,196 --> 00:55:26,991
Thanks for being my shield all this time,

740
00:55:27,575 --> 00:55:28,409
Yoon Yi-jun.

741
00:55:31,954 --> 00:55:33,164
Have a good life.

742
00:55:34,415 --> 00:55:35,958
You finally seem human.

743
00:55:39,420 --> 00:55:41,005
A word, Mr. Yoon.

744
00:55:41,589 --> 00:55:44,133
Please tell us
if this is because of your male secretary.

745
00:55:52,516 --> 00:55:53,517
Excuse me.

746
00:55:54,518 --> 00:55:55,394
Just now…

747
00:55:57,813 --> 00:56:00,024
I'm planning to kidnap you, sir.

748
00:56:00,399 --> 00:56:01,442
We run on three, okay?

749
00:56:03,235 --> 00:56:04,195
One.

750
00:56:05,821 --> 00:56:06,655
-Three.
-Three.

751
00:56:08,032 --> 00:56:10,785
-Wait!
-Wait, sir!

752
00:56:10,868 --> 00:56:12,787
Are you admitting your relationship
with him?

753
00:56:14,455 --> 00:56:15,372
Director Lee!

754
00:56:25,091 --> 00:56:26,092
Hello, my love.

755
00:56:35,267 --> 00:56:36,727
I broke my engagement today.

756
00:56:37,228 --> 00:56:39,772
Do you want to get married, Mr. Ko?

757
00:56:41,232 --> 00:56:43,234
What's your answer?

758
00:56:45,069 --> 00:56:46,862
Are you two lovers?

759
00:56:47,655 --> 00:56:50,699
Did you break off the marriage
because of him? Tell us!

760
00:56:51,117 --> 00:56:53,702
What's your relationship?

761
00:56:53,786 --> 00:56:54,912
What happened?

762
00:57:38,581 --> 00:57:39,748
From now on,

763
00:57:41,167 --> 00:57:42,376
I'm going to stop

764
00:57:43,294 --> 00:57:46,589
hiding and staying quiet.

765
00:57:49,258 --> 00:57:50,384
So,

766
00:57:52,094 --> 00:57:54,471
don't say you don't feel anything
even after 100 times.

767
00:57:56,724 --> 00:57:57,766
Your heart

768
00:58:03,564 --> 00:58:04,899
has to flutter for me.

769
00:59:09,255 --> 00:59:12,049
You dared to hide the accounting manager,

770
00:59:12,132 --> 00:59:13,842
so I wondered how far you'd push it.

771
00:59:14,760 --> 00:59:15,719
We're almost there.

772
00:59:17,888 --> 00:59:21,392
The retained earnings will be restored
before the shareholder meeting.

773
00:59:25,020 --> 00:59:25,980
Who did it?

774
00:59:28,232 --> 00:59:29,858
You already have a good idea.

775
00:59:30,901 --> 00:59:32,528
I'm not going to let Taekang

776
00:59:32,611 --> 00:59:36,740
become the nation's favorite gossip topic
over slush funds or embezzlement.

777
00:59:36,824 --> 00:59:39,410
It sounds like you'll expose it
if things go wrong.

778
00:59:39,493 --> 00:59:41,495
You won't be losing anything
from this deal.

779
00:59:42,579 --> 00:59:43,414
So,

780
00:59:45,124 --> 00:59:46,709
it's up to me?

781
00:59:46,792 --> 00:59:50,879
Taekang is the only thing you love.
You'd hate to see it tarnished.

782
00:59:51,255 --> 00:59:52,965
You should watch your blood pressure.

783
00:59:53,924 --> 00:59:55,342
I'll quietly take care of it.

784
00:59:55,968 --> 00:59:56,802
In return,

785
00:59:58,679 --> 01:00:02,266
I'll marry when I want
and with whom I want.

786
01:00:07,396 --> 01:00:08,897
I love Jae-hee.

787
01:00:09,773 --> 01:00:11,483
So leave her alone.

788
01:00:12,735 --> 01:00:14,111
She's too precious

789
01:00:15,195 --> 01:00:16,447
to even lay a finger on.

790
01:00:40,721 --> 01:00:42,681
THANKS TO CHOI HEE-JIN, KIM DO-YOON,
JUNG YOO-MIN, PARK JUN-MUYN, KIM MIN-GUE

791
01:00:47,186 --> 01:00:49,271
"Do you want to come in
for instant noodles?"

792
01:00:49,688 --> 01:00:51,065
I'm not going to work.

793
01:00:51,148 --> 01:00:52,816
This won't do. This won't do either!

794
01:00:52,900 --> 01:00:54,318
I look too dressed up!

795
01:00:54,401 --> 01:00:57,446
I wanted to do normal things
that other people do.

796
01:00:57,529 --> 01:00:59,239
This isn't a date.

797
01:00:59,323 --> 01:01:01,283
Seems they'll make you
take the fall big time.

798
01:01:01,367 --> 01:01:04,828
With this, you can hand Father
the leash to Yi-jun.

799
01:01:04,912 --> 01:01:06,663
You just need to answer the question.

800
01:01:06,747 --> 01:01:08,624
What if I answer? Can you even handle it?

801
01:01:09,291 --> 01:01:11,043
He'll be in danger at this rate.

802
01:01:11,126 --> 01:01:14,546
And meeting you wasn't luck.
It was a miracle.

803
01:01:16,590 --> 01:01:19,593
Translated by Leo Chung
